       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because 30 mg is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine. The usual adult range is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg is the ceiling. Doses above that raise the risk of marked hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit.\n\nCould this be a typo? These are the likely intended orders:\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the standard starting dose\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum dose\n\nIf you really do intend 30 mg, for example because of an unusual indication, please confirm that with your supervising resident or attending, and I'll enter it with that noted.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
